lines=['# debug.ts latent site census','','Task b5w3ycg. Source/compiler/tool/apply SHA: `e8f3723bd41abcebedabfcc7546fdf104a9bbf08`, the fetched origin/main tip. Both `b4b8c4d7` and `f4e8a4c6` are ancestors, each verified with `git merge-base --is-ancestor` exit 0. TypeScript 6.0.3 source: `050880ce59e30b356b686bd3144efe24f875ebc8`.','','## Run and limitation','','Setup exit 0 (990.636 seconds). `npm ci --prefix stage3/api` exit 0. One `stage3/apply.sh` tree, exit 0 in 1168.566 seconds. Guarded overlay build exit 0 in 641.462 seconds. The same completed tree and binary were used for the measurement.','','Full mode: child exit 0, **50.090 seconds**, **105 units**, zero checker diagnostics. `LATENT_FULL=1`, `LATENT_ONLY_FILE=/workspace/scratch/debug-sites/adapted/src/compiler/debug.ts`, `LATENT_ASSERT_NO_OUTPUT=1`. All other inherited LATENT flags were removed; only LATENT_TIMES was added. Ordinary Load and Lower output guards ran in the actual driver. The raw legacy label `measured on a checker-rejected program` is preserved, despite zero checker diagnostics.','','**First-error was not run.** The pinned tool ignores LATENT_ONLY_FILE in first-error mode: `stage3/census/latent/lower.go.txt:266` iterates every loaded file without `latentFileSelected`; full mode checks that guard in `stage3/census/latent/units.go.txt:119`. The pinned driver loads the compiler directory and its imports. Launching it unchanged would violate debug.ts alone. A question requesting approval for the same selection guard in the scratch first-error overlay remained unanswered while the authorized work completed. No selection patch was applied. Thus no first-error elapsed time, measured first-error stop, or claimed first-error unit count is supplied. This report stops that sub-run at the tool limitation, rather than representing the full run as first-error.','','The first-error source loop treats namespace Debug as one top-level statement; full mode splits nested function declarations. Full mode was used to supply the requested complete site inventory independently of the blocked first-error run. This is the same guarded overlay generation used by the meter and reference core report, with physical generated Go filenames changed only to `.go.txt`. No production source or tool logic was patched.','','The post-apply checkpoint is `1b136f633792e4502b285a3c49d63b0d8a11055b` on `typescript/debug-sites-checkpoint`. The final report branch contains a single commit directly on the pinned main SHA.','','## Forecast sites','','“Gone” below means no finding at that forecast expression in the full-mode stream, including the complete refusal scan. It does not prove each enclosing function lowers: independent generic bodies are deferred and other findings may stop lowering. All forecast coordinates still identify the expected expressions in this adapted tree.','','| Forecast class | Adapted coordinates | Status | Current reason |','| --- | --- | --- | --- |','| 1: assertEachIsDefined marker | 243:59 | Gone | No finding at this expression. |','| 2: first hasProperty(member, ...) | 253:66 | Gone | No finding at this expression. |','| 3: second hasProperty(member, ...) | 253:97 | Gone | No finding at this expression. |']
reason='a value of type (node: Node) => boolean seen as AnyFunction, which can write void where boolean is read'
for l,c,n in [(267,72,'assertEachNode'),(280,98,'assertNode'),(293,108,'assertNotNode'),(307,98,'assertOptionalNode')]:
 s=next(s for s in sites if loc(s)==f'debug.ts:{l}:{c}' and s['phase']=='refusal_scan');assert s['reason']==reason
 lines.append(f'| 4: getFunctionName(test!) in {n} | {l}:{c} | Present, Refused, refusal_scan | {reason} |')
lines+=['| 5: assertEachNode marker and repeats | 268:35, 281:35, 294:35, 308:35, 322:35 | Gone at every listed expression | No finding at these expressions. |','| checkEachDefined marker repeat | line 248 (stackCrawlMark &#124;&#124; checkEachDefined) | Gone | No finding at this expression. |','','The four class-4 stops remain the first refusal-scan wall. Additional lowering findings include the `never` parameter of assertNever and overload implementation compatibility checks before those bodies. Clearing the forecast marker and hasProperty scans therefore does not imply that these declarations now lower completely.','','## Every debug.ts site in source order','','Repeated observations at the same location, kind, exact reason and phase share an F ID. There are 53 such debug.ts sites. The raw stream has 112 findings, including repeated observations, Boundary continuation records, and findings reached in dependencies. `rows.json` retains the observations and recording-unit identities.','','Full mode rolls back failed statements and resumes; downstream “reading” findings may reflect missing locals after rollback. These are observed census findings, not a proven sequence of ordinary compiler stops. Uninstantiated generic units are not proof of successful lowering.','','| Site | Location | Containing declaration | Kind | Exact reason | Phase | Emitting lowering line and deciding function |','| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |']
for s in sites:
 em='; '.join(f"{e['file']}:{e['line']} `{fn(e)}`" for e in emit[s['id']])
 lines.append('| '+' | '.join(cell(v) for v in [s['id'],loc(s),s['owner']['name'] if s['owner'] else '',s['kind'],s['reason'],s['phase'],em])+' |')
lines+=['','## First-wall list','','Exactly the refusal-scan sites, in source order, as requested. This deliberately excludes lowering findings and is not the broader criterion used by the reference core report. Full mode records every scan stop; priority and traversal order can affect the ordinary first stop. There are 11.','']
